---
/** The privacy policy for errantant.com and the Errant Ant app, drafted from how both work today. */
---
<article class="policy">
  <p class="policy-date">Last updated 25 October 2026</p>
  <p>
    Errant Ant is made by Buggy Laggy Limited. This policy covers this website, errantant.com, and the Errant Ant app.
    The app is not released yet; this page describes it as it works today, and we will update it if that changes.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses no cookies, analytics or tracking, and has no forms. Everything it shows loads from errantant.com
    itself; it does not contact any other service.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. To deliver its pages, GitHub receives the information that comes with every
    request, such as your IP address and your browser, and handles it under the <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub
    General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The Errant Ant app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You don't need an account.</li>
    <li>
      Your books, reading history, words, phrases, notes and boards are stored in a folder on your computer. The app
      doesn't send them anywhere, and it contains no analytics or crash reporting.
    </li>
    <li>
      The app goes online only when you ask it to: to fetch Project Gutenberg's catalog and the free books you choose
      from gutenberg.org, and to download a dictionary from GitHub the first time you turn it on. Those services receive
      your requests, including your IP address, under their own privacy policies.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    We don't collect personal data through the website or the app, so we have none to share, sell or delete. What the
    app keeps stays with you: you can delete it at any time with Settings → About → Reset all data, or by deleting the
    app's data folder.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page and the date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:dev@buggylaggy.com">dev@buggylaggy.com</a>.</p>
</article>
